{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on this trip's own trace, and the trace is the field that governs. EV-GPS-02833 records trace_distance_km of 23.22 km between the recorded pickup event (14:53:35) and the recorded dropoff event (15:23:45), against the booking-time optimal of 18.4 km carried on EV-TRIP-02833. That is an excess of 4.82 km, or 26.20% of optimal. Both limbs of the POL-RD-01 gate are passed: 26.20% is greater than the 20% proportional threshold, and 4.82 km is greater than the 0.8 km absolute threshold. I do not rely on the rounded convenience copy trip_record.actual_distance_km of 23.2 for this test, because POL-RD-01 expressly forbids citing it for the threshold test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02833", "EV-TRIP-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes, so no corroboration requirement is imported and no escalation is triggered on this ground. EV-GPS-02833 carries 182 fixes at a 10 second sample interval against a 10 second expected interval, 100.0% coverage, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec of 0.0. None of the POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c) fires: there is no gap over 90 seconds, no straight-line jump over 500 m, and no sustained interval above 30 seconds. The deviation therefore may be, and is, established on the trace alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged on both limbs. (a) Same trip: EV-TRIP-02833, EV-GPS-02833 and EV-FARE-02833 all carry trip_id TRP-02833, and the trip_record started_at of 2026-08-24T14:53:35+08:00 matches the gps_trace first_fix_at to the second, so the artifacts describe the same trip. (b) Excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace: 4.82 km and 26.20% on EV-GPS-02833. The burden then shifts to the driver to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause, and the bare assertion 'Traffic.' points to neither.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02833", "EV-GPS-02833", "EV-FARE-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's traffic excuse cannot be run on this record and must be discarded. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic_advisory that names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, carries a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached that segment, and is matched by a route leaving the corridor before and rejoining after. The only advisory artifact in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02833-01, is MISSING: it has no payload, the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT fired, and its weight_multiplier is 0.0 — I disclose that impairment expressly under POL-GEN-02(1) and cite the artifact only for its absence. No advisory covers the Jurong Point corridor in this window, so the POL-RD-03 comparison is undecidable, the clause is unavailable, and under POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08: it neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an amended optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02833-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's uncited traffic assertion is not an escalation trigger, so the case can and should be decided with money moving. EV-ADVIS-02833-01 is named by no party in support of the excuse; the counterparty statement 'Traffic.' cites no evidence id at all. Under POL-RD-13(1) an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact within POL-RD-10(5) — the absence of an artifact no party has cited is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it. Every other POL-RD-10 trigger is absent too: trip identifiers match across the three artifacts, no pickup or dropoff timestamps disagree, the trace is not impaired, and the refund is well under SGD 150.00 and under charged_total. The rider should therefore receive a monetary partial refund rather than having the amount held on an escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02833", "EV-GPS-02833", "EV-FARE-02833", "EV-ADVIS-02833-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No exculpatory clause on the driver's side is available on the artifacts. EV-CHAT-02833 is COMPLETE with message_count 0 and an empty messages array, so there is no rider instruction that could exonerate any part of the excess under POL-RD-04, and the whole 4.82 km stands. The chat log is likewise the artifact POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 both require, so neither clause can be invoked: there is no detour request to corroborate and no waypoint_hint to test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02833", "EV-TRIP-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02 and runs as follows on the METERED fare. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.4 km = 13.80 distance + 0.28 x 24.8 min = 6.944 time) x the surge_multiplier of 1.0 recorded on EV-FARE-02833, plus 0.80 platform fee, plus 0.00 ERP and tolls on the optimal route, plus 0.00 waiting time fee, less 0.00 promo discount = 25.3440. Refund = charged_total 30.46 less 25.3440 = 5.1160, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 5.15. The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so the outcome is not NO_ACTION, and it is 16.80% of charged_total, well short of the 90% that would make it a FULL_REFUND. The rider's remedy is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 5.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02833", "EV-TRIP-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare carries no pass-through line that could change the figure in either direction, so SGD 5.15 is the complete rider remedy. EV-FARE-02833 shows erp_lines total 0.00, no airport surcharge, waiting_time_fee 0.00 and cancellation_fee 0.00, so there is no off-route gantry to refund as a standalone correction and equally no pass-through line to be double-counted on top of the POL-RD-02 amount — the anti-double-count rule in POL-RD-09(1) is satisfied on these figures.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "One point in the claim as filed is not supported by the record, and I do not press it. The assertion that 'this driver has six deviation flags' rests on driver_profile.prior_deviation_flags on EV-DPROF-02833, which is a LIFETIME counter; POL-RD-06 asks instead for deviation_flags_90d, which on this profile is 0, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting the lifetime counter for the trailing-window one. There is also no PATTERN to establish and no uplift to seek: the measured excess of 26.20% is below the 50% that POL-RD-01 makes a MATERIAL deviation, so POL-RD-06 is not engaged on this trip at all, and the rider's entitlement does not depend on it. It rests on this trip's own trace under POL-RD-01 and on the POL-RD-02 arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02833", "EV-GPS-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own profile does not add any corroboration hurdle here. POL-RD-08 imposes the extra-corroboration condition only where rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1 or fewer. On EV-RPROF-02833 deviation_claims_60d is 1 — below that gate — so the condition does not apply, and in any event the clause states that the factor may never be used to deny a claim that is otherwise proven. The deviation is proven on the trace and the refund follows.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02833"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

